| `make audit-project` `[local]` | Reports what another keel project would fail under this template's gates after `copier update`, on a scratch copy. Its `drift` group reports the recorded template commit, commits behind this checkout (unknown if unresolved), and warnings for settings absent from DEST compared with the current template render. | `make audit-project DEST=../my-project` | [`DEST`](settings.md#make-variables), [`audit_project.settings_tables`](settings.md#configprojectjson) | Missing settings warn because their pre-update absence does not prove owed work afterward. Runs from the template checkout only; in a generated project it names that checkout. It never writes `DEST`. | [generate-and-upgrade.md](../guides/generate-and-upgrade.md) | always |
